From e9cac024659f6102d2297b0ff881a0b438a6748a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian <219239532+markd3ng@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 14:28:33 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(auth): hash BASIC_AUTH with Argon2id and dual-verify
 bcrypt

Context:
Issue #85 (C Argon2id ADOPT_WITH_REDESIGN) requires Worker HTTP
basic-auth hashes to use Argon2id while existing bcrypt BASIC_AUTH
hashes keep verifying. BASIC_AUTH lives in upstream-owned Worker
code, so this is an isolated patch from the pinned upstream SHA.

Expected behavior:
Newly generated BASIC_AUTH hashes are Argon2id (OWASP m=19456,
t=2, p=1). Existing $2a$/$2b$/$2y$ bcrypt hashes still verify.
Unknown prefixes fail closed. Paste management passwords in
shared/verify.ts are unchanged.

Acceptance criteria:
- New hashes start with $argon2id$.
- Existing bcrypt BASIC_AUTH tests still pass.
- Argon2id BASIC_AUTH hashes accept the correct password and reject
  a wrong password.
- Worker-safe implementation: @noble/hashes, not hash-wasm
  (workerd disallows Wasm code generation).
- Do not take a fork lockfile wholesale.

Constraints:
- Generic upstream patch; no Feishu concepts.
- No account system, password-reset, IdP, or credential vault.
- bcrypt-ts remains for bcrypt verify during migration.

Validation:
- TDD: RED hashBasicAuthPassword is not a function; GREEN after
  Argon2id hasher + dual-verify.
- Node v22.23.2 / pnpm 10.28.0
- Tests: 21 files / 157 tests PASS
- lint / typecheck / Prettier PASS
- frontend production build PASS
- wrangler deploy --dry-run PASS

Docs:
- README.md Auth section
- scripts/argon2id.js

Upstream base:
0835cac4ab8f974035d31845f5c2b93b0c85b5c6

Patch ID:
090-argon2id-dual-verify (export after source review)

